Z||000031||batboy||02-03-2000||08:41 PM||||Monkey, I swear sometimes I don't know if you're serious or joking. In case you are really serious and because there are lots of younger folks probably reading this, vinyl is what record albums are (or at least used to be) made from. Sometimes record companies would release a special edition colored vinyl album. Collectors seek these out and are willing to pay premium price for these if they are in excellent to mint condition. I have lots of colored vinyl albums and radio station promo albums that are fairly rare. I have a white vinyl "Beatles White album" and a cool multi-colored marble looking Dave Mason album. ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Scott2M4||02-03-2000||09:04 PM||||All this talk of vinyl reminded me of a movie I used to love so, so, so long ago!  Did anyone ever see the movie <B>Trick or Treat</B>?  Gene Simmons from the band KISS played a radio DJ who got his hands on a demo album of a recently deceased heavy metal rock singer.  He gave the vinyl disc to a high school kid who idolized the singer.  Turns out, the singer's spirit lived in the album and ended up causing mass chaos in the local town.<P>If I'm not mistaken, the band <B>Fastway</B> did the soundtrack ... which kicked a$$!!!!!<P>Oh, those were the days ...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
