Z||000046||ChadMan||02-16-2000||10:32 PM||||I thought I could stay out of this thread, but...<P>Seems like we have a lot of Floyd fans.  Floyd is great.  But I honestly think I like Roger Waters' solo stuff even better.  I believe "Amused to Death" was the greatest rock album of the 90's, and hardly anyone bought it.<P>For the record, the rest of my top 5 albums of the 90's:<P>2. Nirvana "Nevermind"<BR>3. Foo Fighters "Foo Fighters"<BR>4. Oasis "What's the Story Morning Glory"<BR>5. Metallica "Black Album"<P>And I'll always have a soft spot for Johnny Cash, Waylon, Willie and Hank Jr.  Now that's good country (as opposed to anything you hear on country radio today).||||reg||14
